Privacy Policy for OGPA Calculator

Effective Date: January 2026

Introduction

OGPA Calculator ("the App") is designed to help students calculate and track their GPA and OGPA. We respect your privacy and are committed to protecting any information related to your use of the App.

Information We Collect

The App does not collect, store, transmit, or share any personal information with us or any third parties.

The App may store the following information locally on your device:

Student name (if entered by the user)
Subject names
Credits
Grades
GPA and OGPA calculation data
User preferences and settings

All information is stored only on your device and is not transmitted to any external server.

Data Storage

The App uses local device storage to save academic records and settings for user convenience.

Your data remains entirely under your control and is stored only on your device unless you choose to export or back up your information.

PDF Export and Backup

The App allows users to:

Generate PDF reports of academic results
Create local backup files

These files are created and stored locally on your device. The App does not upload these files to any online service.

Internet Connectivity

The App does not require an internet connection for its core functionality.

The App does not send user data to any server.

Third-Party Services

The App does not use:

Analytics services
Advertising networks
User tracking services
External databases
Data Security

Since all information is stored locally on the user's device, users are responsible for protecting access to their devices and backup files.

Children's Privacy

The App does not knowingly collect personal information from children or any users.

Changes to This Privacy Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any updates will be reflected by updating the effective date at the top of this document.

